# Backend Conventions

- ASP.NET Core Web API with Problem Details errors
- Application use cases in module folders; infrastructure behind interfaces
- FluentValidation for request validation
- EF Core with explicit migrations; foreign keys and check constraints
- Non-guessable external IDs in API contracts
- Idempotency keys for sensitive creates; processed-event table for webhooks
- Structured logging with correlation IDs — no document content or secrets in logs
- Integration tests with Testcontainers PostgreSQL for tenant isolation
